camchrome: Windows persona advances in float on the Fontations backend.

The audit's text-scaler row steps the font size by 0.01 px from 20.01 to 22.00 and counts width
changes: ~63% on Linux (a 1/64 px size grid changes on 64% of such steps), nearly all on Windows.
Linux system fonts go through Fontations, whose advance at a size goes through that grid. Under a
Windows persona (CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES, set by the browser in 1018) the advance is read at
ppem == unitsPerEm, a scale of exactly 1, and scaled to the size in float. Unhinted metrics only.

--- a/third_party/skia/src/ports/SkTypeface_fontations.cpp
+++ b/third_party/skia/src/ports/SkTypeface_fontations.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,14 @@
     }();
     return kLevels;
 }
+// camchrome (1021): float design-unit advances (CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES=1).
+bool CamchromeFloatAdvances() {
+    static const bool kOn = [] {
+        const char* v = getenv("CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES");
+        return v && v[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return kOn;
+}
 }  // namespace
 
